/0001819404-26-000051-index.htm","accession":"0001819404-26-000051"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue grew only 2.4% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819404/000181940426000051/0001819404-26-000051-index.htm","accession":"0001819404-26-000051"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-11.9% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819404/000181940426000051/0001819404-26-000051-index.htm","accession":"0001819404-26-000051"},{"text":"Debt of $19.4m against equity of $19.3m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1819404/000181940426000051/0001819404-26-000051-index.htm","accession":"0001819404-26-000051"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 58.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.58,"consecutive":2,"current":0.662,"current_display":"66.2%","threshold_display":"58.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -13.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.13,"consecutive":2,"current":0.024,"current_display":"2.4%","threshold_display":"-13.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this compa